    "<p><span style='background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(20,20,20); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>Brampton Plan-Schedule 6a-Urban River Valley m</span></span>apping depicts the extent of the urban river valley.</p><p>Urban River Valleys are river and stream corridors located within the urban area that provide ecological, recreational, and landscape functions. These valleys contribute to the connectivity of natural systems while offering opportunities for recreation, active transportation, and environmental stewardship.</p><p>This data is intended to be used in conjuction with other related mapping layers for this schedule, and may be impacted by other schedules, with consideration to the text of Brampton Plan.</p>"
